  "scope": "One disposable Kind v1.36.1 control-plane node using kubeadm's local PKI and stacked etcd. A pure planner evaluates each public leaf lifetime under explicit synthetic expiry-offset timestamps and selects the existing server/client/peer command order without changing host time. The case detects a partial renewal, completes kubeadm certificate renewal, restarts the etcd and kube-apiserver static Pods, compares public certificate receipts before/after and live etcd server/peer receipts to renewed files, then writes and reads back a synthetic ConfigMap through the Kubernetes API. A namespaced CronJob makes real not-due and due invocations against the exact public leaf inventory, using explicitly labeled synthetic expiry-offset decision instants; its Pod cannot renew or restart. No private key, token, secret value, external PKI, multi-member behavior, real-clock lead-window scheduling, or production cluster is exercised.",
